course: dictionary
lesson: 3282
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word escape is a good example. «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» Here escape means to get out of a place where you are kept.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «Smoke alarms give families time to escape.» The clues are smoke and alarms, which warn you of danger. So here escape means to get away from danger.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. If you say «Always close farm gates so animals cannot get away», it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If a meaning does not fit, try the next one from the list.
fact: Escape means to get away from a place where you are kept, or from danger.
fact: To escape something means to avoid it, as in «escape the rain».
fact: Gas, water or air escapes when it leaks out of something.
fact: An escape is a way out, such as a fire escape, and Esc is a computer key that cancels.
fact: A word with many meanings is called a multiple-meaning word, and the context shows you which meaning to use.
exercise: «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» What does escape mean here? | Eat all the grass | Grow thick wool | *Get out of a place where they are kept | Sleep in the barn
exercise: Dad says the family must plan an escape route in case of fire. What is an escape route? | *A way out of a building | A route to the shops | A map of the stars | A special kind of fire engine
exercise: Ella says gas escapes from a jar with no lid. What does escapes mean here? | Is burned | Turns into ice | Gets bigger | *Leaks out
test: «Smoke alarms give families time to escape.» What does escape mean here? | Clean the house | Make a loud noise | Stay inside to cook | *Get away from danger
test: On a computer keyboard, what does the Esc key do? | *Cancels | Turns the computer on | Prints a page | Makes the text bigger
exam: A farm sheep «escaped shearing for six years». What does escaped shearing mean? | Got shorn very fast | Was shorn in the rain | *Avoided being shorn | Ran away from the farm
